t of steam. is not because I'm a star, it's because I'm surrounded by stars like yourself who get the need to inject positivity into our politics, who understand that you can make critical points while still being a force multiplier of positive energy and goodness. That's what we do on this show. So every time you see me on another new show like, Oh Jimmy, fail is on again. You should take a little pride of ownership in creating what you've created. You know, because we very much are a movement on this show. We're people who care about the country. I know you're not all Republicans. I know you're not battle acts, you know, politicals who just get out of bed looking for something to hate every day. The vast majority of the people listening to the show just like having a good time and discussing issues that are critical to the country. And there's a lot of you who tune in probably because you've empowered. You listen to me every day and you're like, wow, Jimmy, I could get a show. I could do anything. And that's kind of the hook of Fox across America. It leaves everybody listening, feeling like they too, could get a nationally syndicated talk show. And you might be able to, you never know. But the one guy I am not rooting for in this moment is cocaine Mitch McConnell, who just, I mean, listen, he's going on his vacation this week. And before he does, the swamp is just going to swamp.",
