  {
    "episode_id": 93675,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/3/93675.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 204,
    "turn_text": "Now what Murphy says there, just so we're clear, as he says, the law allows for anyone seeking asylum in our border to come into the country. What he doesn't mention is that Joe Biden made that law. And when I am saying he made that law to be clear, prior to Biden getting in office, the law said Remain in Mexico, meaning any asylum seeker to our border apprehended by authorities would remain in Mexico until their asylum case was heard. This of course was a deterrent. because it took the teeth away from the drug cartels who could no longer guarantee someone entry into the United States of America. By repealing remain in Mexico, Joe Biden handed the power back to the drug cartels to smuggle people into this country because anybody caught gets let in. so when murphy says like well republicans won't give us more funding to deal with these increased numbers he fails to mention that he's the reason his party is the reason we have these increased numbers and we wouldn't have them if instead of funding we actually prioritize the old policies that worked and that's the scam in this moment. Everyone in Washington wants to cover their ass. But do they want to cover people like, oh, I don't know, you, me, or heaven forbid these migrants they purport to care about so much? Not even a little. It is Fox Across America with your main man Jimmy Fela. fight up to talk to this next guest who makes a triumphant return to the show. He's the self-proclaimed best dressed man in Congress. But I have some follow-up on that, but let's just let him walk the catwalk and show us his wares. Representative Wesley Hunt back on the show. Hey, man.",
